{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2646","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2646","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2646\",\"parent_revision\":\"d617d7effa6b16f96db3cbf613b8e94cf31463e882eb5ca9d9d61b45defa1012\",\"root_revision\":\"d617d7effa6b16f96db3cbf613b8e94cf31463e882eb5ca9d9d61b45defa1012\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-08\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe DH plugin currently has a partial workflow graph that captures only decision forks (Mermaid diamond nodes) but not execution steps \u2014 the wrong granularity for two target use cases.\\n\\nAI agents performing impact analysis need to know which actors, steps, MCP calls, and artifacts are affected when a specific skill or reference file changes; without step-level nodes this traversal cannot be done reliably. The current graph also has no mechanism to stay current with repo changes, no incremental update path, and no quality-verified data \u2014 so any graph an agent reads may already be stale or unverified.\\n\\nHuman developers need a navigable map of system responsibilities for comprehension, debugging, and simplification \u2014 the current graph does not support this either.\\n\\nThe gap affects agent workflows (change-propagation analysis, test generation for DH components) and developer understanding alike. A PRD with detailed context is at `.tmp/scratch/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-16T13:48:45.180558Z</sub>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:54:35.979777Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: DH Workflow Extractor System\\nDate: 2026-06-19\\nGoal: Build a machine-readable, always-current actor-step graph of the DH plugin's workflow that supports AI agent impact analysis and human developer comprehension.\\nConditions:\\n1. Outer traversal strategy | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User accepted 2026-06-19 \u2014 deterministic enumeration (enumerate_scope.py) + full ensemble per file\\n2. Storage architecture | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User accepted 2026-06-19 \u2014 DH-owned JSON in docs/workflow-layers/*.json; optional UA export\\n3. Consumer interface | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User accepted 2026-06-19 \u2014 /dh:workflow-query skill + existing explorer HTML\\n4. claude -p in git hook context | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 hooks.json Claude Code lifecycle only; SessionStart adopted\\n5. Current component state | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 plan_ensemble.py and reduce.py in plugin-creator; workflow-extractor agents absent\\n6. UA graph schema | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 224 nodes, 7 types, zero step-type nodes\\n7. Full reachable file set | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Computed by enumerate_scope.py during implementation\\n8. Post-commit hook design | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User accepted 2026-06-19 \u2014 SessionStart staleness check (meta.json vs HEAD)\\n9. reduce.py change strategy | Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User accepted 2026-06-19 \u2014 contribute upstream to plugin-creator\\n10. Workflow-extractor agents confirmed absent | Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker verified\\n11. Idempotency of incremental pipeline | Final: DERIVABLE | Verifiable during implementation\\nAVAILABLE count: 9\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-worker.md` \u2014 NEW agent to create; haiku fleet worker that extracts step-centric relationships from a single source file using one rule group slice | Risk: HIGH | Why: Does not exist; must be created from scratch with 9 step-centric rule groups replacing prior fork-centric rules; incorrect rules produce incorrect graph data consumed by downstream consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` \u2014 NEW agent to create; sonnet verifier that performs evidence-quote grounding per finding and logs misses to `.tmp/extraction-misses/` | Risk: HIGH | Why: Does not exist; must implement active evidence check (\u226580% quote match), CONFIRMED/PLAUSIBLE/REFUTED verdict system, and miss log \u2014 passive verify mode predecessor had no evidence grounding\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor.md` \u2014 currently listed in KNOWN_ENTITIES.md as a canonical agent name but removed from `agents/` (confirmed by commit `fix(dh): remove fabricated workflow-extractor agents`); this orchestrator role is replaced by `workflows/dh-extract-file.js` | Risk: HIGH | Why: The agent is retired; KNOWN_ENTITIES.md still lists it as canonical; any system referencing `subagent_type=\\\"dh:workflow-extractor\\\"` will fail at dispatch time\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/workflows/dh-extract-file.js` \u2014 NEW dynamic workflow script to create; replaces the retired orchestrator agent; args: `{ source_file, layer_type, report_dir? }`; orchestrates plan_ensemble.py \u2192 N haiku workers \u2192 reduce.py \u2192 sonnet verifier \u2192 merge_layer.py | Risk: HIGH | Why: Does not exist; is the new central coordination point for extraction; must invoke `-p` / headless Claude Code without Skill() calls; failure here halts all extraction\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` \u2014 NEW Python script to create; BFS crawler from entry point SKILL.md files; produces `docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md` | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Does not exist; deterministic (no LLM), but scope errors cause extraction to miss files or include non-DH files; the scope file is the input gate for the post-commit hook\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/merge_layer.py` \u2014 NEW Python script to create; reads existing layer JSON, removes all items where `item.source_file == fragment.meta.source_file`, appends fragment items, writes back | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Does not exist; idempotency requirement is a correctness constraint \u2014 a bug here produces layer data corruption across re-extraction runs\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md` \u2014 NEW file produced by `enumerate_scope.py`; consumed by post-commit hook as the in-scope file filter | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Does not exist; post-commit hook depends on it; stale or missing SCOPE.md causes hook to either miss changed files or trigger extraction on out-of-scope files\\n\\n- `hooks/post-commit` (or prek equivalent) \u2014 NEW hook to create; fires after every commit, diffs HEAD~1 HEAD, intersects with SCOPE.md, triggers `dh-extract-file.js` per changed file | Risk: HIGH | Why: Does not exist; this is the automation heartbeat for graph freshness; wrong intersection logic silently skips changed files without any error signal; must not block the commit\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/plan_ensemble.py` \u2014 consumed by `dh-extract-file.js` as the deterministic map-side step; invoked as `plan_ensemble.py extraction-rules.json --window 4 --json`; PRD marks it correct with no changes | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: plan_ensemble.py lives in the `plugin-creator` plugin, not the DH plugin; the workflow script will reference it via an absolute or CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT-relative path that must resolve correctly in headless `-p` context where plugin paths differ from session context\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` \u2014 consumed by `dh-extract-file.js` as the reduce-side bookend; requires 2 changes: (1) slug-normalised heading keys when no line number, (2) cross-group signal (`cross_group: true`) for findings corroborated by \u22652 rule groups | Risk: HIGH | Why: reduce.py is shared infrastructure in the `plugin-creator` plugin; the 2 changes alter corroboration output shape; any other consumer of reduce.py (ensemble-rule-review skill) must remain compatible with the changed output schema\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` \u2014 currently assembles `dh-workflow-graph.json` from the L0\u2013G8 layer JSON files; PRD marks its role as \\\"unclear\\\" under the new crawl-based design where the graph is built incrementally | Risk: HIGH | Why: If the new system produces step-layer JSON files, assemble_graph.py must be extended to parse step nodes (which requires markdown parsing, not just JSON); step nodes also reference artifacts, actors, and MCP calls not in the current L0/L1 schema \u2014 the assembler may produce an invalid or incomplete graph\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 renders `dh-workflow-graph.json` via Cytoscape.js; PRD identifies that step nodes, hook nodes, and new edge types (`gap`, `loads`, `stores_in`, `triggered_by`) require UI changes | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: New node types and edge types will silently not render if the explorer's node/edge type handlers are not updated; gap edges (amber dashed) require specific rendering logic for the AI trust signal to be visible\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/extraction-rules.json` \u2014 currently has 6 fork-centric rules; must be replaced with 9 step-centric rule groups | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the primary input to plan_ensemble.py for the DH extraction workflow; wrong rules produce worker output that misses steps, over-reports forks, and does not corroborate step-level findings; the entire extraction quality depends on rule correctness\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` \u2014 the assembled output graph; will require rebuild after any extraction run or assembler change | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: This is consumed by dh-workflow-explorer.html and by any AI agent querying the graph; stale graph between extraction passes produces incorrect impact analysis; the new incremental update model means the graph is rebuilt piecemeal, which could produce inconsistent intermediate states\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 lists `workflow-extractor`, `workflow-extractor-reducer`, `workflow-extractor-worker` as canonical agent names; the orchestrator (`workflow-extractor`) is retired and replaced by a JS workflow; `workflow-extractor-worker` and `workflow-extractor-reducer` are new agents to be created | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The file lists all three as canonical; agents that do not exist in `agents/` will fail at dispatch; any extraction worker that validates against this list will resolve an entity to a non-existent agent; the file is a living document and must be updated when agents are added or renamed\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-schema.md` \u2014 aspirational schema document, confirmed diverged from the PRD data model; must be rewritten to match PRD node types (decision, step, agent, skill, reference_file, mcp_tool, artifact, backend, hook) and edge types (branch, next, defers_to, dispatches, calls, reads, writes, loads, stores_in, triggered_by, gap) | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Stale schema document misleads agents and developers who read it to understand the graph format; incorrect schema descriptions produce wrong assembler implementations\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/G1-failure-modes.json`, `G2-artifacts.json`, `G3-actor-types.json`, `G4-concurrency.json`, `G5-optionality.json`, `G6-task-types.json`, `G7-complexity-routing.json`, `G8-backend-routing.json`, `L0-forks.json`, `L1-trace-*.json` \u2014 existing layer data; PRD retains these as enrichment to annotate step and mcp_tool nodes; they carry fork-centric data collected in prior passes | Risk: LOW | Why: No changes to these files are required; they are kept as enrichment; risk is that `assemble_graph.py` must correctly merge them with the new step layer without overwriting them\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-result.json` \u2014 present in docs/; relationship to dh-workflow-graph.json unclear; may be an intermediate or legacy artifact | Risk: LOW | Why: Not mentioned in PRD; likely legacy but should be verified before implementation begins to confirm it is not consumed by any live system\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- No tests identified for any of the existing workflow extraction scripts (`assemble_graph.py`, `plan_ensemble.py`, `reduce.py`) or for the proposed new scripts (`enumerate_scope.py`, `merge_layer.py`). The PRD's success criteria include idempotency, incremental isolation, and deterministic output \u2014 all of which are testable properties \u2014 but no test files are specified. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Three critical correctness properties (idempotency, incremental isolation, deterministic output) have no test coverage; a bug in merge_layer.py that fails idempotency would corrupt accumulated layer data on the second extraction run and is invisible without a test\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` \u2014 currently references `dh:workflow-extractor` (haiku model) as the extraction agent in the Tier 2 update process and in the collection methodology section; the PRD changes the model to `sonnet` for the verifier and retires the orchestrator agent in favour of a JS workflow | Risk: HIGH | Why: COVERAGE.md is the first file any agent or developer reads before any collection pass; if it continues to reference the retired `dh:workflow-extractor` agent with wrong model, agents will attempt to dispatch a non-existent agent and the update process instructions will be incorrect\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` \u2014 references \\\"wrong dispatch mechanism\\\" per PRD; contains the extraction pipeline description and agent roles | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is a CLAUDE.md rule file loaded into every session in the DH plugin directory; stale agent references (workflow-extractor as Claude agent instead of JS workflow) will cause any developer or agent following the rules to attempt incorrect workflows; the rule currently says \\\"Extraction agents are pending redesign (see PRD)\\\" but must be updated post-implementation with the correct dispatch reference\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 describes the extraction pipeline using `dh:workflow-extractor` (sonnet orchestrator), `workflow-extractor-worker` (haiku), `reduce.py --keep-threshold 2`; this description matches the pre-PRD design; post-implementation this file must describe the JS workflow as orchestrator, the 9-group rule schema, and the active evidence check | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: This methodology document is cited by COVERAGE.md and used by agents performing collection passes; stale orchestrator description causes mismatched extraction\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 \\\"Adding skills or agents\\\" section references `/dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` as the update step; this skill pointer is still correct post-implementation, but the CLAUDE.md documentation update triggers table will need to reflect that step-node extraction uses the new JS workflow, not the old agent | Risk: LOW | Why: The skill pointer itself is valid; risk is limited to the update trigger table becoming partially stale for step-node changes\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/meta-workflow-graph-refresh/SKILL.md` \u2014 currently points to COVERAGE.md and workflow-trace-methodology.md; the skill body is a pointer only (\\\"Read them in order\\\") with no embedded process steps; no change needed to the skill itself | Risk: LOW | Why: The skill's instructions are pointer-based; it will automatically pick up correct content once COVERAGE.md and workflow-trace-methodology.md are updated\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 declares SessionStart, TaskCompleted, PostToolUse (Write|Edit|Bash), SubagentStop, SessionEnd handlers; the new post-commit hook must be registered here or via prek (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`) | Risk: HIGH | Why: If the post-commit hook is not registered in the correct hooks manifest, it will never fire; `hooks.json` handles Claude Code lifecycle events (not git hooks); a git post-commit hook must be registered separately in prek or git hooks \u2014 conflating the two would cause silent failure of the auto-refresh trigger\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 auto-discovers agents from `agents/`; `workflows/` is not a standard auto-discovered path; the new `dh-extract-file.js` in `workflows/` must be declared explicitly if it requires plugin-level registration | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The plugin.json declares mcpServers but not a workflows key; if JS workflow invocation requires a plugin manifest entry, the file must be updated; if not, the workflow file is invoked directly as a script with no registration needed\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` / prek \u2014 the post-commit hook is a git lifecycle event, not a Claude Code hook; it must be declared in prek or `.git/hooks/post-commit`; this repo uses `prek` (pre-commit replacement) | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The PRD is ambiguous about hook registration: \\\"prek equivalent\\\" suggests prek, but prek manages pre-commit hooks, not post-commit; native git hook at `.git/hooks/post-commit` or a prek `post-commit` stage may be required; wrong registration means the hook never fires\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 root dev-dependencies must mirror PEP 723 declarations for `enumerate_scope.py` and `merge_layer.py`; `ruamel.yaml` is required for YAML operations per repo conventions | Risk: LOW | Why: If PEP 723 deps are declared in the scripts but not mirrored in root dev-group, ty/ruff/IDE will report unresolved imports; not a runtime failure but a tooling compliance issue\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 instructs extraction workers to validate every extracted entity name against this list; lists `workflow-extractor` as a canonical agent name that no longer exists as an `agents/*.md` file; workers that validate against this list will accept `workflow-extractor` as a valid entity even though it cannot be dispatched | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Living document protocol says workers must add new entities before emitting findings; if the orchestrator role is retired and the JS workflow is not listed as an entity, workers have no canonical name to reference for the orchestration actor\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 instructs agents performing collection passes on the ensemble pipeline using the old agent-based orchestrator; any agent following this methodology will spawn the wrong orchestrator | Risk: HIGH | Why: AI-facing methodology document; agents read this file to perform collection; stale orchestrator instructions produce incorrect dispatch attempts\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` \u2014 instructs any agent working in the DH plugin context on how to run extraction; currently says \\\"Extraction agents are pending redesign (see PRD)\\\"; after implementation, must provide the correct JS workflow invocation path | Risk: HIGH | Why: Rule file is loaded into every session in the DH plugin directory; incorrect post-implementation instructions actively mislead agents\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-worker.md` | Role: producer | Connection: new worker agent to create; core extraction actor for haiku fleet | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` | Role: producer | Connection: new verifier agent to create; active evidence check + miss log | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor.md` | Role: producer | Connection: retired orchestrator agent; replaced by JS workflow; must be removed and KNOWN_ENTITIES updated | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/workflows/dh-extract-file.js` | Role: producer | Connection: new JS workflow to create; central orchestration of extraction pipeline | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` | Role: producer | Connection: new Python script; BFS scope crawler producing SCOPE.md | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/merge_layer.py` | Role: producer | Connection: new Python script; incremental layer JSON update | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md` | Role: other-reference | Connection: new file produced by enumerate_scope.py; consumed by post-commit hook | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `hooks/post-commit` (prek or native git) | Role: configuration | Connection: new hook; triggers extraction on commits that change in-scope files | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/plan_ensemble.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: invoked as map-side by dh-extract-file.js; no changes needed to the script but invocation path must resolve in headless context | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'plan_ensemble'\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: invoked as reduce-side; requires 2 output schema changes (slug keys, cross_group flag) | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'reduce\\\\.py'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: assembles dh-workflow-graph.json; role unclear under new design; may require extension for step node parsing | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` | Role: consumer | Connection: renders graph JSON; step nodes, hook nodes, new edge types require UI changes | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/extraction-rules.json` | Role: producer | Connection: primary input to plan_ensemble.py; must be replaced with 9 step-centric groups | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'extraction-rules'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: vocabulary oracle for workers; lists retired agent as canonical; must be updated | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-schema.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: aspirational schema document; diverged from PRD data model; must be rewritten | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: first-read file for any collection pass; references retired agent with wrong model | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'dh:workflow-extractor'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: rule file loaded into every DH plugin session; references wrong dispatch mechanism | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'workflow-extractor'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: describes extraction pipeline for agents performing collection passes; stale orchestrator reference | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'workflow-extractor'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` | Role: configuration | Connection: DH plugin hook manifest; post-commit hook must be registered in the correct system (prek/git, not Claude Code hooks) | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Role: configuration | Connection: auto-discovers agents; `workflows/` directory is non-standard and may require explicit registration | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` | Role: other-reference | Connection: assembled output consumed by explorer and AI agents; requires rebuild after extraction | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `pyproject.toml` | Role: configuration | Connection: root dev-deps must mirror PEP 723 blocks in enumerate_scope.py and merge_layer.py | Action: CONFIG_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: update trigger table for step-node changes; skill pointer to meta-workflow-graph-refresh remains valid | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `dh-extract-file.js` / extraction pipeline \u2014 entire new orchestration layer with no prior implementation; headless `-p` context constraint blocks Skill() calls, requiring custom agent dispatch patterns\\n  - `reduce.py` \u2014 shared cross-plugin script; output schema changes affect both the DH extraction system and the existing ensemble-rule-review consumers in plugin-creator\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` + `COVERAGE.md` + `workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 three AI-facing documents that will actively mislead extraction agents until updated; corrections are blocking for any agent attempting a collection pass post-implementation\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - migration (new JS workflow replaces Claude agent orchestrator with different invocation constraints)\\n  - compatibility (reduce.py output schema change crosses plugin boundary into plugin-creator)\\n  - scope (post-commit hook registration mechanism is unresolved \u2014 prek vs native git hook)\\n  - verification (no tests for any deterministic scripts, critical idempotency property is untested)\\n  - documentation (three AI-facing documents reference the retired agent; stale until updated)\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` \u2014 not described in original item; the change to reduce.py crosses into the plugin-creator plugin and affects all ensemble-rule-review consumers; requires coordination with that plugin's consumers\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 identified as requiring UI changes for new node/edge types; scoped separately per PRD but must be tracked as a dependent deliverable\\n  - Post-commit hook mechanism (prek vs native git hook) \u2014 unresolved architectural decision with direct impact on the hook registration system; must be resolved before implementation\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\n### Concerns\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n\\nThe DH Workflow Extractor system directly supports the plugin's stated mission as a \\\"language-agnostic development process harness.\\\" The system makes the harness's own process more observable and analyzable to AI agents and human developers \u2014 a core infrastructure goal aligned with the design principle \\\"the harness owns the process.\\\"\\n\\nThe proposed extraction design (crawl-based, step-level granularity, quality-verified findings, incremental updates) follows established DH patterns:\\n- Workflow introspection via graph-based system documented in recent merges (commit ce34c666, CLAUDE.md hooks, meta-workflow-graph-refresh skill)\\n- Artifact registration for system outputs (consistent with artifact conventions in CLAUDE.md lines 130\u2013160)\\n- MCP-native approach to discovery and storage (aligns with \\\"every stage produces MCP-registered artifact\\\" principle)\\n\\nThe cross-plugin reference to `ensemble-rule-review` infrastructure (reduce.py, plan_ensemble.py) is valid composition \u2014 DH correctly scopes its own workflow extraction while leveraging shared utility infrastructure. This does not expand DH's scope beyond its stated mission; it localizes extraction to DH's internal processes.\\n\\nThe proposed system imposes no novel human checkpoints and produces no changes to the 7-stage pipeline, role resolution, or dispatch pattern. Dispatch architecture notes (-p mode limitation on skills, workflow script agent dispatch) are documented constraints, not design violations.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **dh workflow extractor system** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User PRD \u2014 .tmp/scratch/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:8eff124303c475d569ecc18236699149 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-16)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:47:38.251344Z</sub>\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a feature item. No existing broken behavior to reproduce.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:48:07.938679Z</sub>\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 P2 could-have. The absence does not break existing workflows, but AI agent impact analysis and DH test generation are both blocked without step-level graph data. The decision forks captured by the current graph are the wrong granularity for both use cases, and the graph has no mechanism to stay current. Deferring this means every change-propagation assessment and DH test-generation attempt must proceed without a reliable actor-step map.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:48:39.325753Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Blocks**: AI agent impact analysis for DH plugin changes (no reliable actor-step traversal); DH component test generation (agents cannot enumerate what each component does, calls, or depends on); human comprehension of responsibility distribution across the plugin.\\n- **Bottleneck**: Any agent doing change propagation analysis on a DH skill or reference file must approximate impact without a step-level graph \u2014 incorrect blast-radius assessments and missed side effects are the failure mode. The current `dh-workflow-graph.json` has 224 nodes, 7 types, and zero `step`-type nodes. Developers reading the existing graph see decision forks only, not the execution steps that compose each workflow.\\n- **Stale graph risk**: No mechanism keeps the current graph synchronized with HEAD. An agent consuming the graph after any skill or agent change reads stale data with no staleness signal.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:49:10.511624Z</sub>\\n\\n- AI agents can perform accurate change-propagation analysis: \\\"if I modify skill X, which actors, steps, MCP calls, and artifacts are downstream?\\\"\\n- DH component test generation becomes tractable: the graph exposes what each component does, what it calls, and what it depends on \u2014 sufficient to write targeted tests for any part of the system.\\n- Graph stays current automatically: SessionStart staleness check fires re-extraction for changed in-scope files, eliminating manual refresh.\\n- Quality is observable: every node carries a `verified` status and a source citation; unverified transitions are marked as gap edges so consumers know what is uncertain.\\n- Human developers gain a navigable responsibility map for comprehension, debugging, and simplification \u2014 not just a decision-fork diagram.\\n- Incremental updates: re-extracting one source file does not touch nodes contributed by other files; one changed skill triggers one file's worth of work.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:49:39.693692Z</sub>\\n\\nThe workflow graph contains `step`-type nodes with actor attribution, MCP call lists, artifact reads/writes, and dispatch links. Every step node carries a `verified` field and a source citation (file path, heading, verbatim evidence quote) that resolves against the current repo HEAD.\\n\\nTransitions that could not be confirmed by evidence appear as `gap` edges (dashed, marked unverified) rather than being silently omitted. An AI agent traversing the graph from any node can enumerate all downstream actors, MCP calls, and artifacts, with gap edges clearly distinguishing verified from unverified paths.\\n\\nWhen an in-scope source file changes, the next Claude Code session's SessionStart hook detects the staleness (by comparing `meta.json.last_analyzed_commit` to HEAD), re-extracts only the changed file's fragment, and merges it into the layer JSON without altering contributions from other files. `COVERAGE.md` is updated to reflect the new extraction state.\\n\\nThe `/dh:workflow-query` skill accepts natural-language impact queries from AI agents and returns graph traversal results (affected nodes, edge types, verification status). The existing `dh-workflow-explorer.html` renders the updated graph for human developers.\\n\\nRe-extracting the same source file twice with unchanged content produces identical layer JSON (idempotent merge). Scope enumeration terminates: `enumerate_scope.py` follows all four reference types up to a depth of 15 and writes a flat `SCOPE.md`; the reachable file set is deterministic and reproducible.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:50:14.487024Z</sub>\\n\\n1. After extraction runs against at least one DH reference workflow file, `docs/workflow-layers/step.json` contains at least one node with `\\\"type\\\": \\\"step\\\"`. (Current state: zero step-type nodes in the graph \u2014 verified 2026-06-19.)\\n\\n2. For a known source file (e.g. `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md`), every step node extracted from that file has a `source_file` matching the file path, a `source_heading` matching an actual heading in the file, a `verified` boolean, and a non-empty `evidence` field containing a verbatim quote from the file at that heading. Spot-check at least three nodes manually against the source file.\\n\\n3. Re-extracting the same source file with unchanged content produces the same `step.json` contents as the previous extraction run \u2014 verified by comparing JSON after two sequential runs (idempotency check).\\n\\n4. Modifying one in-scope source file and running extraction updates step nodes attributed to that file without altering step nodes attributed to any other source file \u2014 verified by diffing layer JSON before and after, confirming `source_file != modified_file` nodes are unchanged.\\n\\n5. The `dh-workflow-graph.json` (or assembled graph) contains gap edges (`\\\"type\\\": \\\"gap\\\"`) for at least one transition that could not be fully attested by evidence quotes. Gap edges are rendered visibly distinct (e.g. dashed amber) in `dh-workflow-explorer.html` and are returned with a `verified: false` flag by `/dh:workflow-query`.\\n\\n6. `/dh:workflow-query` is loadable by an agent and accepts an impact query (e.g. \\\"what is downstream of skill X?\\\") and returns a non-empty list of downstream node IDs, edge types, and verification statuses for at least one real skill node in the graph.\\n\\n7. After modifying an in-scope source file and starting a new Claude Code session, the SessionStart hook detects the change (file appears in `git diff {last_analyzed_commit} HEAD --name-only` AND is in `SCOPE.md`) and triggers re-extraction without requiring a manual command. `COVERAGE.md` reflects the updated extraction timestamp for that file.\\n\\n8. `COVERAGE.md` accurately reflects the extraction state: each in-scope file has an entry showing the last extraction date, verified node count, and unverified node count. The values match what is stored in the corresponding layer JSON fragment metadata.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:51:29.061882Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| PRD | `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/.tmp/scratch/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` \u2014 fact-checked v4 amended; full scope, 9 extraction rule groups, data model, fragment ETL design, resolved design decisions |\\n| Existing script | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/plan_ensemble.py` \u2014 ensemble worker assignment (in plugin-creator, not DH) |\\n| Existing script | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` \u2014 corroboration reducer (in plugin-creator, not DH) |\\n| Existing graph | `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` \u2014 current 224-node, 7-type graph; zero step-type nodes |\\n| Existing docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 canonical entity vocabulary |\\n| Existing docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-schema.md` \u2014 aspirational schema, diverged from actual graph |\\n| Existing docs | `plugins/development-harness/COVERAGE.md` \u2014 per-file extraction state (has model error to fix) |\\n| Existing skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/meta-workflow-graph-refresh/SKILL.md` \u2014 manual entry point for graph refresh |\\n| Existing rule | `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` \u2014 references incorrect agent names |\\n| Existing UI | `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 human graph viewer; reused for step-node rendering |\\n| Skill | `/plugin-creator:ensemble-rule-review` \u2014 extraction ensemble conventions and worker/reducer patterns |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:42:24.027335Z</sub>\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:50:49.341003Z</sub>\\n\\nNew files to create:\\n\\n| Path (relative to plugin root) | Role |\\n|---|---|\\n| `scripts/enumerate_scope.py` | Deterministic reachable-file-set computation; writes `docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md` |\\n| `scripts/merge_layer.py` | Fragment ETL \u2014 reads layer JSON, removes old items for changed source file, appends new fragment, writes back |\\n| `workflows/dh-extract-file.js` | Dynamic workflow orchestrator: plan_ensemble \u2192 haiku workers \u2192 reduce \u2192 sonnet verifier \u2192 merge_layer |\\n| `agents/workflow-extractor-worker.md` | Haiku extraction worker; applies one rule slice to one source file; emits YAML findings |\\n| `agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` | Sonnet verifier; reads ranked findings from reduce.py; emits CONFIRMED/PLAUSIBLE/REFUTED per finding; writes miss log |\\n| `docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md` | Flat list of reachable files with entry point and reference type |\\n| `docs/workflow-layers/meta.json` | Tracks `last_analyzed_commit` for staleness detection |\\n| `docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` | Vocabulary oracle: canonical agent, skill, MCP tool, artifact names |\\n| `skills/workflow-query/SKILL.md` | `/dh:workflow-query` \u2014 programmatic graph query skill for AI agents |\\n\\nFiles to modify:\\n\\n| Path | Change |\\n|---|---|\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` | Contribute two corroboration improvements: slug-normalised heading keys; cross-group location signal. Upstream contribution \u2014 verify backward-compat first. |\\n| `docs/extraction-rules.json` | Replace 6 fork-centric rules with 9 step-centric rule groups |\\n| `docs/graph-schema.md` | Rewrite to match PRD data model (step, hook node types; gap, dispatches, calls edge types) |\\n| `COVERAGE.md` | Fix haiku\u2192sonnet model annotation for workflow-extractor; add per-file extraction state columns |\\n| `.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` | Update to reflect SessionStart trigger (replaces incorrect post-commit hook reference) and correct agent names |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:51:54.411441Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Depends on**: None \u2014 RT-ICA APPROVED with no missing blockers. All five design decisions resolved 2026-06-19.\\n- **Cross-plugin coupling**: `reduce.py` and `plan_ensemble.py` live in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/`, not in DH. The two corroboration improvements (slug-normalised heading keys; cross-group location signal) must be contributed upstream to plugin-creator. If backward-compat verification fails, a thin DH wrapper is the fallback \u2014 forking is not permitted.\\n- **Blocks**: Any backlog item that requires AI agent impact analysis on DH plugin changes or DH component test generation. No existing open items are directly gated on this completing.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-19T16:52:21.840608Z</sub>\\n\\n**High** \u2014 new system with no existing tests, spanning multiple components across two plugins.\\n\\nContributing factors:\\n- Two new Python scripts with correctness requirements (enumerate_scope.py graph traversal up to depth 15; merge_layer.py idempotent fragment ETL).\\n- One new dynamic workflow script (dh-extract-file.js) coordinating deterministic and LLM steps.\\n- Two new agents from scratch (workflow-extractor-worker with 9 rule groups; workflow-extractor-reducer with miss logging).\\n- One new skill (/dh:workflow-query) with agent query interface.\\n- Schema rewrite (graph-schema.md, extraction-rules.json).\\n- Cross-plugin upstream contribution to reduce.py with backward-compat verification required before merge.\\n- SessionStart hook integration for staleness detection.\\n- No existing tests for any of the deterministic scripts; tests need to be written from scratch.\\n- Open implementation decisions remain for assemble_graph.py scope and L0-G8 data migration path (do not block planning but add surface area).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-03T01:21:54.038686Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Plan \u00a78.3 mandated the two reduce.py changes (slug-normalised heading keys, cross_group) ship \\\"behind a backward-compat gate\\\" (flag/version check), but the shipped reduce.py has no such gate \u2014 the new heading-slug branch in `normalize_location()` runs unconditionally for every caller (argparse only exposes report_dir/--glob/--keep-threshold). Needs a design decision on the gate mechanism, tied to the same cross_group redesign already flagged above. (found by /code-review max --fix pr, verified independently twice)\\n- [ ] merge_layer.py's `merge_fragment()` removes every layer edge tagged with a re-extracted source_file, but `ExtractionFragment` has no `edges` field to re-add them \u2014 edges attributed to a re-extracted file are permanently deleted on every re-extraction with no restoration path. The module's own docstring frames this as deliberate (ownership deferred to dh-extract-file.js, which doesn't exist yet), but as shipped this is real, current data loss with no owner. Needs either an `edges` field on ExtractionFragment, or an explicit decision that per-file layers never carry edges (in which case the removal step should not run either). (found by /code-review max --fix pr, verdict PLAUSIBLE \u2014 deliberate-per-docstring but unowned)\\n- [ ] The `gap` edge type (verified=false, gap=true, \\\"required for correct impact-radius analysis\\\" per architect spec) is entirely unimplemented in assemble_graph.py: `_edge()`'s `verified`/`gap` parameters are accepted but no call site ever overrides their defaults, and `gap_count` in the assembled output is a hardcoded `0`. graph-schema.md now documents gap-edges as a first-class concept but no code path can ever produce one. Likely T18's scope (\\\"verify step-node/next-edge handling; extend or document any gaps\\\") \u2014 flagging explicitly so it isn't missed. (found by /code-review max --fix pr, verdict CONFIRMED)\\n- [ ] reduce.py's new heading-slug normalization in `normalize_location()` changes corroboration keying for the external cross-plugin consumer at examples/solid-review-ab/runner/scorer.py (imports normalize_location via importlib). That consumer's tests/docstrings still describe the pre-change contract (\\\"returns stripped input when no line number is present\\\") and neither test_scorer.py nor test_scorer_independent.py exercises the new branch \u2014 a false-green on out-of-date test coverage. Impact is bounded/latent today (the gold corpus is all line-numbered), but the external contract is now undocumented drift. Needs the scorer.py docstring/tests updated to match, or the change scoped so it can't reach that consumer. (found by /code-review max --fix pr, verdict CONFIRMED)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Wave 0 Research Dh Workflow Extractor System\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSynthesized from PRD (draft v4, 2026-06-15) which cites direct source reads of:\\nplan_ensemble.py, reduce.py, graph-schema.md, COVERAGE.md, workflow-extractor agents,\\nplugin.json, hooks.json, work-backlog-item SKILL.md, groom/swarm.md, add-new-feature SKILL.md,\\nimpact-analyst.md, claude-plugins-reference-2026, claude-skills-overview-2026, ensemble-rule-review SKILL.md\\n\\n### API State \u2014 Existing Extraction Infrastructure\\n- `plan_ensemble.py`: exists, described as correct, no changes needed per PRD\\n- `reduce.py`: exists, needs 2 changes (slug-normalised heading keys, cross-group signal)\\n- `workflow-extractor-worker.md`: exists but has wrong rules (fork-centric, not step-centric)\\n- `workflow-extractor-reducer.md`: exists with passive verify mode (needs active evidence check + miss log)\\n- `workflow-extractor.md` (orchestrator): exists but uses wrong primitive (Claude agent vs JS workflow)\\n- `assemble_graph.py`: exists, role unclear under new crawl-based design\\n- `extraction-rules.json`: has 6 fork-centric rules, needs replacement with 9 step-centric groups\\n- `graph-schema.md`: aspirational, diverged from PRD data model\\n\\n### Ecosystem Research \u2014 UA Integration\\n- UA (`~/repos/understand-anything`) provides: fingerprinting (SHA-256 per file), change-classifier (SKIP/PARTIAL/ARCHITECTURE/FULL), post-commit hook pattern, batch merge with gap recovery\\n- UA has already run against DH plugin: `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` (224 nodes, 411 edges)\\n- UA dashboard renders DH agents as `service` nodes, MCP tools as `endpoint` nodes \u2014 6 overlays matching proposed design\\n- UA `article-analyzer` extraction NOT suitable: no verbatim evidence quotes, uses LLM judgment for edge weight (same failure mode as rejected INFERRED edges)\\n\\n### Impact Measurement \u2014 Current State vs Target\\n- Current graph captures only decision forks (Mermaid diamonds) \u2014 confirmed wrong granularity\\n- No incremental update path exists: full rebuild required on any change\\n- No quality verification: no verified/unverified status per node\\n- COVERAGE.md has a model error: references haiku for dh:workflow-extractor (should be sonnet)\\n- `.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` references wrong dispatch mechanism\\n\\n### Codebase Audit \u2014 Missing Components\\n- `scripts/enumerate_scope.py`: does not exist \u2014 must be created\\n- `scripts/merge_layer.py`: does not exist \u2014 must be created\\n- `workflows/dh-extract-file.js`: does not exist \u2014 must be created (replaces orchestrator agent)\\n- `docs/workflow-layers/SCOPE.md`: does not exist \u2014 created by enumerate_scope.py\\n- Post-commit hook (prek equivalent): does not exist \u2014 must be created\\n\\n### Open Architectural Decisions (not resolvable by research)\\n1. Crawl-based outer loop \u2194 ensemble per-file pipeline composition: architectural choice\\n2. Storage: build on UA graph vs separate DH layer vs hybrid: architectural choice\\n3. Consumer interface: UA dashboard vs query skill vs session-start injection: product choice\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVerification run: 2026-06-16  \\nClaims verified: 10  \\nVerdicts: 4 REFUTED, 6 VERIFIED  \\nCritical blockers: 3\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Refuted Claims\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### 1. dh-workflow-graph.json captures only decision forks\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED  \\n**Source:** `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`  \\n**Finding:** Node types present: decision=121, agent=28, artifact=14, backend=4, mcp_tool=23, reference_file=20, skill=14. **Zero step-type nodes exist.** The graph structure does NOT include step nodes at all \u2014 claiming they are \\\"absent or minimal\\\" is false because the node type itself is not defined in the schema.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. plugins/development-harness/scripts/plan_ensemble.py exists\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED  \\n**Source:** Filesystem search in `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/scripts/`  \\n**Finding:** File NOT found in development-harness scripts directory. Actual location: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/plan_ensemble.py` \u2014 belongs to plugin-creator, not development-harness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. plugins/development-harness/scripts/reduce.py exists\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED  \\n**Source:** Filesystem search in `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/scripts/`  \\n**Finding:** File NOT found in development-harness scripts directory. Actual location: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` \u2014 belongs to plugin-creator, not development-harness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. workflow-extractor.md and workflow-extractor-worker/reducer.md exist in agents/\\n**Verdict:** REFUTED (both files)  \\n**Source:** Filesystem search in `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/`  \\n**Finding:** Zero files matching workflow-extractor* pattern found. All three agent files referenced in the PRD (orchestrator, worker, reducer) do not exist. The agents were never created or have been removed.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verified Claims\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- \u2713 SCOPE.md does NOT exist (as expected)\\n- \u2713 enumerate_scope.py does NOT exist (to be created)\\n- \u2713 merge_layer.py does NOT exist (to be created)\\n- \u2713 COVERAGE.md references haiku as model for dh:workflow-extractor (model error confirmed)\\n- \u2713 .understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json exists with 224 nodes, 411 edges (exact match)\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rtica Blocking Findings\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Condition 1: Path assumption error**  \\nPRD places `plan_ensemble.py` and `reduce.py` in DH scripts, but both are in plugin-creator/ensemble-rule-review. Implementation path must correct this location mismatch before proceeding.\\n\\n**Condition 2: Graph baseline is false**  \\nExisting dh-workflow-graph.json (224 nodes total) contains ZERO step-type nodes. The PRD's step-extraction design is architecturally sound but assumes a false baseline about the current graph structure. The current graph captures decisions and other entity types, but not steps.\\n\\n**Condition 3: No prior workflow-extractor agents**  \\nAll three workflow-extractor agents (orchestrator, worker, reducer) referenced in PRD have never been created. This indicates the PRD design is based on a prior conversation or design iteration that was planned but never implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Impact:** 3 conditions BLOCK planning until assumptions are corrected. Recommend rtica-assessor review and determine whether PRD scope is modified or clarified before task planning proceeds.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d87705713f44305248bc8fdfa0a6715da07c913aaaa1e3dfabe4b1c208d913eb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJbFw\"}"}